        "## 1. My rule and its reason codes\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Signal checks, my rule, and its reason code\n",
        "\n",
        "### Lane confirmation\n",
        "\n",
        "I confirm my lane as **Refresh / Content Opportunity Scoring**.\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal is to rank content pages for human refresh review using observable search-performance and freshness signals.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Signal 1 — staleness behind refresh flags\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question:** Are pages that have not been updated for at least 91 days more likely to show decline than recently updated pages?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Verdict: CONFIRMED**\n",
        "\n",
        "In this dataset, the 91+ day group has a higher observed decline rate than the 0–90 day group. This supports using staleness as a directional refresh-review signal, but it does not prove that age causes decline.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Signal 2 — volume behind quick-win logic\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question:** Are pages with at least 100 impressions more likely to have measurable decline than very low-volume pages?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Verdict: CONFIRMED**\n",
        "\n",
        "Pages with at least 100 impressions have a higher observed decline rate than pages with fewer than 100 impressions. Volume also makes the decision more useful because a refresh on a visible page has more potential impact.\n",
        "\n",
        "### My baseline rule\n",
        "\n",
        "A page receives a refresh-review action when:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. `days_since_last_update >= 91`, and\n",
        "2. `impressions_90d >= 100`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Eligible pages are ranked by their impressions percentile. I use staleness as a threshold rather than rewarding extreme age because the rule should remain simple and readable.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each row receives exactly one reason code:\n",
        "\n",
        "* `stale_visible_page` when both conditions hold\n",
        "* `below_refresh_threshold` otherwise\n",
        "\n",
        "The action label is:\n",
        "\n",
        "* `REFRESH_REVIEW` for eligible pages\n",
        "* `MONITOR` for other pages\n",
        "\n",
        "The score uses only `days_since_last_update` and `impressions_90d`. It does not use `trend_direction`, `trend_pct`, the label, or any 30-day comparison window.\n"
      ],
